WEBVTT

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:30.570
The review app runs on this computer and needs no internet.

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:36.160
The demo opens with invented chat exports already imported.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:40.210
Anita enters her name so each edit records who made it.

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:46.830
The Imports tab lists each chat export that was read.

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:52.190
Opening one shows the original text, untouched, with line numbers.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:56.300
The Kumar Builders order is one message on lines 6 to 9.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:03.090
The Orders tab suggests messages that mention catalogue products.

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:09.660
Draft order prepares a draft from the Kumar Builders message.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:14.970
Prices come from the catalogue. The draft total is INR 28,355.20.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:19.580
No open issues are flagged. A later correction is not yet linked.

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:26.880
Each field has source labels that show where its value came from.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:33.410
Clicking Chat line 7 on the product field highlights the word cement.

00:01:33.410 --> 00:01:37.800
The quantity label highlights the exact words 40 bags cement.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:45.790
Anita links the later message, "Sorry make it 45 bags cement."

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:53.790
She gives a reason: "Customer corrected cement to 45 bags."

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:03.040
She excludes the old 40-bag line. The total is now INR 30,979.20.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:07.650
Accepting the order locks it. The page reads Accepted and frozen.

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:14.160
Export uses only orders that a person has accepted.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:19.620
The CSV carries the corrected 45 bags, not the original 40.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:26.470
A Zoho Books import file is prepared. It is not yet tried in Zoho.

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:31.140
Tally Prime refuses until each name is matched in export-map.json.

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:37.480
The dashboard states its dates: 2026-01-12 to 2026-01-21.

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:42.250
It shows the gap as well: no data for 16 to 19 January.

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:47.390
It refuses a week comparison: "Insufficient comparable data".

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:52.060
By default it counts accepted orders: INR 30,979.20 on 2026-01-12.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:57.910
Follow-ups list what is still open in the chats.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:02.100
Meera Shah's quote request is listed as open.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:06.190
Promised and reported payments are listed as things to check.

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:10.690
A promise or a report is not a verified payment, the page says.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:18.420
A coding agent uses MCP, a tool link, to load the catalogue.

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:28.720
It imports a Hindi-English chat. Each draft line cites its chat words.

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:36.720
Its proposed edit is recorded as agent:demo-agent, with a reason.

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:46.060
Export refuses: nothing is accepted. The agent has no accept tool.
